{"line": "header", "transcript": "03-duplicate-record-replay", "demonstrates": "Duplicate records are safe. A resumed run re-emits an already-collected object with identical content, and then emits the same object twice within the run. Both duplicates reconcile to one current Note with no byte change and no new Note ID.", "gate": "a2-normative", "operation": "collect", "mode": "incremental", "expected_outcome": "complete", "expected_exit_code": 0, "notes": "Over-collection is the safe direction: a cursor that lags may replay records, and portable-source-key reconciliation makes replay idempotent. Under-collection is not safe, which is why a cursor may never advance past an undurable write."}
{"line": "core", "action": "resume", "detail": "Core replays a cursor that deliberately lags the durable state, as it would after a crash between a durable write and a checkpoint commit."}
